;; `(-> Int64 (GIter Int64))` → CDZ0203. So the bug is solve_recursive_params writing an over-nested `f`.
;; MECHANISM (traced in collect_param_constraints / arg_ty_in_env, infer.rs:3548/4014):
;;   - gmap body = `GIter.Cons(f(h), gmap(rest, f))`. `f(h)` unifies f's var to `(-> h_ty ?result)` with
;;     ?result FRESH (3642-3663, the fn-param-applied-as-head arm) — CORRECT so far.
;;   - The `GIter.Cons(f(h), gmap(rest,f))` result ties `f(h)`'s ?result to Cons's element `a`, and the
;;     recursive self-call `gmap(rest, f)` must unify into Cons's `(GIter a)` tail.
;;   - THE OVER-NEST: `arg_ty_in_env(gmap(rest,f))` — gmap is a DEF (not a scheme-op, not a param), so
;;     binder_var_of=None and scheme_of=None → it FALLS THROUGH to `type_of(db, arg)` (infer.rs:4157),
;;     which types the self-call via the normal apply_type path using gmap's OWN in-flight/partial scheme.
;;     Typing `gmap(rest, f)` mid-solve re-applies gmap's `(GIter a)→(a→b)→(GIter b)` with `f`'s result var
